<feed> tree:member <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/GBX/current/T4000001/1/> .
<http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/GBX/current/T4000001/1/>
    a skos:Concept ;
    dc:isVersionOf <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/collection/GBX/current/T4000001/>;
    dc:modified '2010-03-23T14:50:17'^^xsd:dateTime ;
    skos:altLabel ''^^xsd:string ;
    skos:prefLabel 'File format page - info text'@en ;
    skos:definition '''{"node": {
    "p": [
        "In most cases, data are available in three data file formats. To assist your decision, a brief summary of the available formats is provided below",
        "Please select your preferred data file format from the available options below and use the \'Submit\' button to proceed."
    ],
    "ul": {"li": [
        "ASCII - a BODC output format that contains several rows of metadata followed by the data cycles (data variables and their quality control flags) listed one per line.",
        "ODV - the SeaDataNet Ocean Data View (ODV) data format - an ASCII format that follows that of a spreadsheet containing metadata, primary variable and data columns. ODV is a software package for the interactive exploration, analysis and visualisation of oceanographic and other geo-referenced profile or sequence data.",
        "QXF - the BODC subset of netCDF. QXF is \'a format for datacycles\'. Consequently, it does not include the metadata. Each QXF file contains a header (a series of global attributes) and a series of QXF channels. These channels generally consist of a data variable plus quality control flag channel, although the flag channel will not be encountered in some circumstances."
    ]}
}}'''@en ;
    skos:notation 'SDN:GBX::T4000001'^^xsd:string .
